.Dd $Mdocdate: September 20 2026 $
.Dt BTD.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm btd.conf
.Nd Bluetooth daemon configuration file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Xr btd 8
daemon keeps the Bluetooth devices listed here connected.
.Pp
Macros can be defined that will later be expanded in context.
Macro names must start with a letter, digit, or underscore,
and may contain any of those characters.
Macro names may not be reserved words.
Macros are not expanded inside quotes.
.Pp
Addresses are written as six colon separated hexadecimal octets, most
significant first.
For LE devices this is the address the device advertises while
pairing.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic device Ar ugenN
Use this
.Xr ugen 4
device instead of the first Bluetooth controller found.
.It Ic firmware Ar name
Load the firmware from
.Pa /etc/firmware/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa _fw
and
.Pa /etc/firmware/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa _config .
By default the name follows from the USB vendor and product.
.It Ic hid Ar address
Connect to an LE HID device, such as a keyboard or a mouse, and send
its input to
.Xr wscons 4 .
Up to eight may be given.
.It Ic headset Ar address Op Brq ...
Stream the
.Xr sndiod 8
mix to an A2DP headset.
Only one headset is supported.
The following options may be given in braces:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic bitpool Ar number
Upper bound of the SBC bitpool, 2 to 53, lowered to what the headset
accepts.
The default is 53.
.It Ic rate Ar 44100 | 48000
Sampling rate.
48000 falls back to 44100 if the headset lacks it.
The default is 48000.
.El
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/btd.conf -compact
.It Pa /etc/btd.conf
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
hid 00:11:22:33:44:55
hid 00:11:22:33:44:67
headset 00:11:22:33:44:77 {
	rate 48000
	bitpool 53
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr btctl 8 ,
.Xr btd 8
.Sh CAVEATS
Some LE devices, such as Logitech keyboards and mice, advertise a new
address each time they enter pairing mode, and may distribute a
different identity address once paired.
.Xr btd 8
stores the identity address with the bond and recognizes the device by
either address, but a device paired again must have its
.Ic hid
line updated to the address it advertised while pairing.
